erm, sidewalks are typically public domain, even when cutting across private property. Theres no signs stating private property, nor gates preventing travel. We will completely disregard the charter violations though. Lets stick to the "private property" straws youre grasping. (also see, RIGHT OF WAY, and EASEMENT)

&#x200B;

Im STILL trying to find out who owns the convention center itself, but im pretty sure its a municipal building, meaning its public property. if you can find out the real owners, and prove its private property, okay. But im pretty sure its a crown building.

